# J3 — Explicit-target consent (PR #64 promise)
# Persona: user sitting in a repo dir runs bare `kuzushi`. The picker may
# OFFER cwd as a row but must require an explicit Enter; Esc opts into
# targetless browsing; nothing silently falls back to cwd.
# Launch 1 takes the Esc (decline) path, launch 2 the explicit-Enter path.
name: Explicit-target consent
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
snap: picker-offers-cwd
expect: Nothing defaults to cwd silently
expect: git repo
ask: Is "you are about to scan THIS directory" unmistakable — does the cwd row identify the directory clearly?
keys: Escape
wait: 3
snap: after-esc-targetless
ask: After Esc — is the shell honestly targetless (no silent cwd fallback in the status chrome), and does it say how to pick a target later?
submit: quit
wait: 2
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
keys: Enter
wait: 3
snap: after-explicit-enter
ask: After explicit Enter on the cwd row — does the status chrome now show the chosen target, and is it clearly the result of MY explicit consent (not a default)?
